{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"REBAR-DEBUG — root cause PROVEN; Phase 2 repair BLOCKED at the caller-dependency gate.\n\n## Proven root cause (single cause; explains every symptom)\n\n`rebar.llm.plan_review.review_plan` resolves the gate handle at `plan_review/__init__.py:439`\nbut does NOT pass it into `_run_plan_review`, and `gate_source.annotate_result` stamps\n`verdict[\"source\"]` only at line 452 — i.e. AFTER `_run_plan_review` has already signed at\nlines 706-734. The sign condition (lines 706-711) gates on `sign` / `verdict == PASS` /\n`runner != \"exempt\"` / `coverage.llm_ran is not False`, and has NO source in scope at all,\nso the local-source never-sign invariant cannot be enforced there.\n\nThe same invariant IS implemented on the completion side — `_commands/transition_close.py:392-398`:\n\n    # local source (opt-in back-out) verified + passed but is NEVER signed (epic\n    # raze-vet-ditch S4: an unattested run produces no signature).\n    if result.get(\"source\") == \"local\":\n        return None\n\n…because on that path `result[\"source\"]` is already populated when the sign decision runs.\nPlan-review is the surface that missed the guard.\n\n`verified_at_sha=None` is the same cause, not a second one: attested mode records the pinned\nsnapshot SHA; a local read has no pinned SHA.\n\n## Proof (discriminating experiment, runtime oracle)\n\nInstrumented the sign-decision site and ran a local-source review. At the moment the sign\nbranch is taken:\n\n    DEBUG sign_site: sign=True verdict='PASS' runner='pydantic_ai' source=None\n                     source_key_present=False\n                     keys=[advisory, blocking, coaching, coverage, dropped, indeterminate,\n                           material_fingerprint, model, overflow, runner, ticket_id,\n                           ticket_type, triage, verdict]\n    DEBUG sign_branch_TAKEN\n    final verdict source='local' signed=True\n\nThis KILLED the obvious competing fix: a guard written as `verdict.get(\"source\") != \"local\"`\nat line 706 would be a SILENT NO-OP — the key is absent there. The guard must read the\nresolved source/handle, not the verdict. Instrumentation reverted; worktree clean.\n\n## Legitimacy: `defect` (multi-sourced authority, no ambiguity)\n\n- `docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md:119` (design authority) — \"`source=local`\n  remains the documented back-out to the prior in-place read (never signs).\"\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:76-77` (module contract) — \"``local`` reads the\n  in-place checkout (dirty allowed, never signed).\"\n- `src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:51` (CLI help) — \"local: read the in-place checkout\n  (dirty allowed, never signs)\".\n- `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py:392-398` (sibling implementation, epic\n  raze-vet-ditch S4).\n\n## BLOCKER — caller-dependency gate: DO NOT auto-fix\n\n`tests/conftest.py:218-232` is an AUTOUSE fixture that defaults the ENTIRE offline suite to\n`REBAR_GATE_SOURCE=local`, because disposable tmp_path repos have no `origin` remote and\nattested would (correctly) fail closed. Local-source signing is therefore load-bearing for a\nlarge share of the suite.\n\nMeasured with a prototype guard (`sign and handle.source != \"local\"`), then reverted:\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py` — 30 failed / 37 passed\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/` (whole dir)      — 47 failed / 315 passed\n\nThese are real behavioral dependencies, not incidental usage. The fix is feasible but is a\ntest-infrastructure change, not a one-line guard. Note `transition_close.py` already shows the\noffline-safe attested recipe: `source=\"attested\", ref=\"HEAD\", fetch=False` resolves from the\nLOCAL object DB with no remote.\n\n## The choice (needs a decision before Phase 2 proceeds)\n\n- **(A)** Fix the guard AND migrate the suite's offline default to attested/`ref=HEAD`/\n  `fetch=False` so signature-dependent tests keep working. Correct per ADR 0005; touches an\n  autouse fixture and ~47 lifecycle tests.\n- **(B)** Fix the guard and give the suite an explicit test-only signable-local opt-in. Smaller\n  blast radius, but it keeps a \"local can sign\" path alive in code.\n- **(C)** Decide local-source signing is intended for plan review, and correct ADR 0005, the\n  snapshot contract, and the CLI help instead. Cheapest, but it documents a gate bypass:\n  a dirty worktree could still mint a claim-valid attestation with verified_at_sha=None.\n\nRecommendation: (A). No code changed on this ticket.\n\n## Incidental finding (separate from this bug)\n\nAC5 of epic 58f2 also asserts exempt-type results remain unsigned. They do not: a `bug`\nticket reviewed on current main returns `runner='pydantic_ai'` (NOT `exempt`), runs a full\nreview, and signs. Harmless today — the claim gate exempts bugs anyway — but the\n`runner != \"exempt\"` guard at `plan_review/__init__.py:709` is not doing what AC5 assumes."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784937697777369001,"uuid":"18ff26e3-2f47-4f00-a736-e2596a25d34b"}